let skill_group_2 : Array[SkillFile] = [
  {
    skill: "serbox-move-repo",
    path: "SKILL.md",
    body: "---\nname: serbox-move-repo\ndescription: Use when the user wants to move the repository they are working in into a serbox box - \"move this repo to a box\", \"continue this work in the box\", \"copy my project into serbox\". Copies the checkout, its worktrees, uncommitted and stashed work, then installs dependencies inside the box.\nmetadata:\n  installed-by: serbox\n---\n\n# Move a local repository into a serbox box\n\nThis moves the git checkout of the current directory into one box and leaves\nthe local copy untouched. After it finishes the box has the same HEAD, index,\nbranches, stashes and worktrees, plus untracked files that git does not ignore.\nConversation history from agent tools is **not** copied; this skill only moves\nthe repository.\n\nPaths in the examples assume this skill is installed at\n`~/.agents/skills/serbox-move-repo` (or `~/.claude/skills/...`); adjust `S` if\nyours is elsewhere.\n\nPrerequisites: `git`, `tar`, `node` (for the file plan) and a working `serbox`\nbox. Run the steps in one shell session so `S`, `ROOT`, `BOX` and `DEST` stay\nset.\n\n## 1. Pick the box and destination\n\n```sh\nset -euo pipefail\nS=\"$HOME/.agents/skills/serbox-move-repo/scripts\"\nROOT=\"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\"\nBOX=\"${BOX:-work}\"\nDEST=\"${DEST:-/data/home/$(basename \"$ROOT\")}\"\nserbox get \"$BOX\" >/dev/null || serbox create --name \"$BOX\" --template alpine\n```\n\nIf the box does not exist, create it with the template the project needs\n(`ubuntu`, `node`, `python`, ...; see `serbox templates`). A wrong template\nmeans missing runtimes later.\n\n## 2. See the plan\n\n```sh\nnode \"$S/repo-files.mjs\" --json \"$ROOT\"\n```\n\nThe plan lists the files that will move and the size. Build output and\ndependency directories (`node_modules`, `target`, `dist`, `.venv`, caches, ...)\nare skipped even when they are untracked; **tracked** files are always kept so\n`git status` matches. Use `--keep NAME` to include an excluded directory by\nliteral name (for example a source tree that really lives in `build/`).\n\nBefore moving, tell the user:\n\n- Git push and pull will not work in the box until credentials are configured\n  there; environment secrets and git config are separate steps (see the\n  `serbox-basic-setup` skill).\n- Copying `.git/config` copies any remote URL, including an embedded token.\n- Untracked `.env` files that git ignores are **not** copied. Move their values\n  with `serbox secrets set`, never by printing them.\n\n## 3. Copy the repository and its git data\n\n```sh\nnode \"$S/repo-files.mjs\" --list0 \"$ROOT\" > /tmp/serbox-move.list\ntar -C \"$ROOT\" --null -cf /tmp/serbox-move.tar -T /tmp/serbox-move.list\ntar -C \"$ROOT\" -rf /tmp/serbox-move.tar .git\nserbox push \"$BOX\" /tmp/serbox-move.tar /tmp/serbox-move.tar\nserbox exec \"$BOX\" -- sh -c \"mkdir -p '$DEST' && tar -xf /tmp/serbox-move.tar -C '$DEST' && rm /tmp/serbox-move.tar\"\nrm -f /tmp/serbox-move.list /tmp/serbox-move.tar\n```\n\nThe second `tar -rf` adds `.git` (all branches, stashes, index and worktree\nmetadata) while the file list stays manageable. If the user does not want git\nhistory in the box, omit that line and add `--no-git` when running\n`move.sh` below.\n\n## 4. Verify and install dependencies\n\n```sh\nserbox exec \"$BOX\" --workdir \"$DEST\" -- 'git status --short; git log -1 --oneline'\nbash \"$S/deps.sh\" \"$BOX\" \"$DEST\"\n```\n\n`deps.sh` detects `package.json`, lockfiles, `Cargo.toml`, `go.mod`,\n`requirements.txt`, `pyproject.toml` and `Gemfile`, and runs the matching\ninstall command with the tool already present in the box. It does not install\nmissing runtimes; if a tool is absent, tell the user which template or package\nto add.\n\n## Shortcut\n\n`move.sh` wraps steps 3 and 4:\n\n```sh\nbash \"$S/move.sh\" \"$ROOT\" \"$BOX\"            # keeps .git, installs deps\nbash \"$S/move.sh\" \"$ROOT\" \"$BOX\" --no-git   # code only\n```\n\nThe box and the local checkout are independent after the move. Nothing keeps\nthem in sync; later changes need another `push` or a git remote.\n",
  },
  {
    skill: "serbox-move-repo",
    path: "scripts/deps.sh",
    body: "#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Install a moved project's dependencies inside a serbox box.\n# usage: deps.sh BOX DIR\nset -euo pipefail\nbox=\"${1:?usage: deps.sh BOX DIR}\"\ndir=\"${2:?usage: deps.sh BOX DIR}\"\nrun() { serbox exec \"$box\" --workdir \"$dir\" -- \"$@\"; }\nhave() { serbox exec \"$box\" -- \"command -v '$1' >/dev/null 2>&1\"; }\n\nif serbox exec \"$box\" -- \"test -f '$dir/package.json'\"; then\n  if serbox exec \"$box\" -- \"test -f '$dir/pnpm-lock.yaml'\"; then\n    have pnpm && run pnpm install --frozen-lockfile || echo \"note: pnpm is not installed in the box\"\n  elif serbox exec \"$box\" -- \"test -f '$dir/yarn.lock'\"; then\n    have yarn && run yarn install --frozen-lockfile || echo \"note: yarn is not installed in the box\"\n  elif serbox exec \"$box\" -- \"test -f '$dir/package-lock.json'\"; then\n    have npm && run npm ci || echo \"note: npm is not installed in the box\"\n  else\n    have npm && run npm install || echo \"note: npm is not installed in the box\"\n  fi\nfi\n\nif serbox exec \"$box\" -- \"test -f '$dir/Cargo.toml'\"; then\n  have cargo && run cargo fetch || echo \"note: cargo is not installed in the box\"\nfi\nif serbox exec \"$box\" -- \"test -f '$dir/go.mod'\"; then\n  have go && run go mod download || echo \"note: go is not installed in the box\"\nfi\nif serbox exec \"$box\" -- \"test -f '$dir/requirements.txt'\"; then\n  have python3 && run python3 -m pip install -r requirements.txt ||\n    echo \"note: python3/pip is not installed in the box\"\nfi\nif serbox exec \"$box\" -- \"test -f '$dir/pyproject.toml'\"; then\n  have python3 && run python3 -m pip install -e . ||\n    echo \"note: python3/pip is not installed in the box\"\nfi\nif serbox exec \"$box\" -- \"test -f '$dir/Gemfile'\"; then\n  have bundle && run bundle install || echo \"note: bundler is not installed in the box\"\nfi\n",
  },
  {
    skill: "serbox-move-repo",
    path: "scripts/move.sh",
    body: "#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Copy a git checkout into a serbox box (shortcut for the steps in SKILL.md).\n# usage: move.sh REPO BOX [--dest PATH] [--no-git]\nset -euo pipefail\nroot=\"${1:?usage: move.sh REPO BOX [--dest PATH] [--no-git]}\"\nbox=\"${2:?usage: move.sh REPO BOX [--dest PATH] [--no-git]}\"\nshift 2\ndest=\"\"\ngit=1\nwhile [ $# -gt 0 ]; do\n  case \"$1\" in\n    --dest) dest=\"${2:?--dest needs a path}\"; shift 2 ;;\n    --no-git) git=0; shift ;;\n    -h|--help) sed -n '2,3p' \"$0\"; exit 0 ;;\n    *) echo \"move.sh: unknown argument $1\" >&2; exit 2 ;;\n  esac\ndone\nS=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\" && pwd)\"\nroot=\"$(git -C \"$root\" rev-parse --show-toplevel)\"\n[ -n \"$dest\" ] || dest=\"/data/home/$(basename \"$root\")\"\nwork=\"$(mktemp -d)\"\ntrap 'rm -rf \"$work\"' EXIT\n\nnode \"$S/repo-files.mjs\" --list0 \"$root\" > \"$work/files\"\ntar -C \"$root\" --null -cf \"$work/repo.tar\" -T \"$work/files\"\nif [ \"$git\" = 1 ]; then\n  tar -C \"$root\" -rf \"$work/repo.tar\" .git\nfi\nserbox push \"$box\" \"$work/repo.tar\" /tmp/serbox-move.tar >/dev/null\nserbox exec \"$box\" -- sh -c \"mkdir -p '$dest' && tar -xf /tmp/serbox-move.tar -C '$dest' && rm /tmp/serbox-move.tar\"\nif [ \"$git\" = 1 ]; then\n  serbox exec \"$box\" --workdir \"$dest\" -- 'git status --short'\nfi\nbash \"$S/deps.sh\" \"$box\" \"$dest\"\necho \"moved $root to $box:$dest\"\n",
  },
  {
    skill: "serbox-move-repo",
    path: "scripts/repo-files.mjs",
    body: "#!/usr/bin/env node\n// Plan which files of a git checkout move into a serbox box.\n// Prints names and sizes only; never reads file contents.\nimport { spawnSync } from 'node:child_process';\nimport { existsSync, statSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport { join, resolve } from 'node:path';\n\nconst EXCLUDED_DIRS = new Set([\n  'node_modules', 'target', 'dist', 'build', 'out', '.next', '.nuxt',\n  '.svelte-kit', '.turbo', '.cache', 'coverage', '__pycache__', '.venv',\n  'venv', '.tox', '.mypy_cache', '.pytest_cache', '.gradle', '.idea',\n  '.vscode', 'bazel-bin', 'bazel-out', 'bazel-testlogs', '.dart_tool',\n  '.terraform', '.serverless', '.parcel-cache', '.angular', '.expo',\n]);\n\nfunction usage(message) {\n  if (message) process.stderr.write(`repo-files: ${message}\\n`);\n  process.stderr.write('usage: repo-files.mjs [--json|--list0] [--keep NAME] [ROOT]\\n');\n  process.exit(2);\n}\n\nconst argv = process.argv.slice(2);\nlet mode = 'json';\nlet keep = new Set();\nlet rootArg = '';\nfor (let i = 0; i < argv.length; i++) {\n  const a = argv[i];\n  if (a === '--json') mode = 'json';\n  else if (a === '--list0') mode = 'list0';\n  else if (a === '--keep') {\n    if (i + 1 >= argv.length) usage('--keep needs a name');\n    keep.add(argv[++i]);\n  } else if (a === '-h' || a === '--help') usage();\n  else if (a.startsWith('-')) usage(`unknown option ${a}`);\n  else if (!rootArg) rootArg = a;\n  else usage(`unexpected argument ${a}`);\n}\n\nconst cwd = resolve(rootArg || '.');\nconst root = spawnSync('git', ['-C', cwd, 'rev-parse', '--show-toplevel'], {\n  encoding: 'utf8',\n});\nif (root.status !== 0) usage(`${cwd} is not inside a git checkout`);\nconst rootDir = root.stdout.trim();\n\nconst listed = spawnSync(\n  'git',\n  ['-C', rootDir, 'ls-files', '-z', '--cached', '--others', '--exclude-standard'],\n  { encoding: 'buffer', maxBuffer: 1024 * 1024 * 512 },\n);\nif (listed.status !== 0) {\n  process.stderr.write(listed.stderr?.toString() || 'git ls-files failed\\n');\n  process.exit(1);\n}\n\nconst parts = listed.stdout.toString('utf8').split('\\0').filter(Boolean);\nconst tracked = new Set(\n  spawnSync('git', ['-C', rootDir, 'ls-files', '-z', '--cached'], {\n    encoding: 'buffer',\n    maxBuffer: 1024 * 1024 * 512,\n  }).stdout.toString('utf8').split('\\0').filter(Boolean),\n);\n\nfunction excluded(rel) {\n  const segments = rel.split('/');\n  for (const segment of segments) {\n    if (EXCLUDED_DIRS.has(segment)) return !keep.has(segment);\n    if (/\\.egg-info$/.test(segment) || /^bazel-/.test(segment)) {\n      return !keep.has(segment);\n    }\n  }\n  const base = segments[segments.length - 1];\n  if (/\\.(o|so|pyc|pyo|class|dylib|dll|exe|a)$/.test(base)) {\n    return !keep.has(base);\n  }\n  return false;\n}\n\nconst files = [];\nlet bytes = 0;\nfor (const rel of parts) {\n  if (!tracked.has(rel) && excluded(rel)) continue;\n  const full = join(rootDir, rel);\n  if (!existsSync(full)) continue;\n  let size = 0;\n  try {\n    size = statSync(full).size;\n  } catch {\n    continue;\n  }\n  files.push({ path: rel, size, tracked: tracked.has(rel) });\n  bytes += size;\n}\n\nif (mode === 'list0') {\n  process.stdout.write(files.map((f) => f.path).join('\\0') + '\\0');\n} else {\n  const skipped = parts.length - files.length;\n  process.stdout.write(\n    JSON.stringify({\n      root: rootDir,\n      total: files.length,\n      bytes,\n      skipped,\n      excludedDirs: [...EXCLUDED_DIRS].sort(),\n      files,\n    }, null, 2) + '\\n',\n  );\n}\n",
  },
]

///|
let skill_group_3 : Array[SkillFile] = [
  {
    skill: "serbox-snapshots",
    path: "SKILL.md",
    body: "---\nname: serbox-snapshots\ndescription: Use when the user wants to save a serbox box's state and load it later - \"save a snapshot\", \"checkpoint this box\", \"restore from a snapshot\", \"start a new box from my setup\", \"clone this box\". Covers serbox snapshot save/ls/restore/rm/import, fork and create from a saved image.\nmetadata:\n  installed-by: serbox\n---\n\n# serbox snapshots: save, restore, fork\n\nA snapshot is a Docker image made from a box with `docker commit`. It contains\nthe box's whole filesystem: system files, installed packages and `/data`\n(including `HOME`). It does **not** contain running processes, memory, open\nconnections or host-side port forwards. A box restored from a snapshot is a\npower-cut copy: files are exactly as they were, processes are not running.\n\nSnapshots stay on the machine, need no registry and no account. They are listed\nunder `~/.serbox/snapshots` (or `SERBOX_HOME`) and stored as local Docker\nimages tagged `serbox-snapshot/<name>:latest`.\n\n## Save\n\n```sh\nserbox snapshot save work --name work-ready --description \"deps installed\"\nserbox snapshot save work                    # name: work-<timestamp>\nserbox snapshot ls\n```\n\n- A running box is committed live. The command waits for Docker to finish, so\n  when it returns the snapshot is ready. Stop the box only when a program must\n  flush its data first (a database mid-write); `docker commit` also works on a\n  stopped box.\n- Names are 1 to 80 characters from `a-z`, `A-Z`, `0-9`, `.`, `_` and `-`, must\n  start with a letter or digit, and cannot start with `sn_` or `im_`. They must\n  be unique on the machine.\n- A snapshot can contain credentials that applications wrote to disk (git\n  credentials, cloud CLI state, `.netrc`, shell history). Treat a snapshot as\n  sensitive: do not publish or share the machine's images without review.\n\n## Restore and load\n\n```sh\nserbox snapshot restore work --snapshot work-ready --yes   # in place\nserbox create --name work2 --snapshot work-ready           # a new box\nserbox fork work --name work2 --count 2                    # copies of a box\n```\n\n`snapshot restore` replaces the box's container with the snapshot image. The\nbox keeps its name, `--env` values, secret names and published ports, but every\nfile changed since the snapshot is lost. Without `--snapshot` it uses the most\nrecent snapshot whose source is that box.\n\n`create --snapshot NAME` creates a new box from a snapshot without touching the\nsource. `fork BOX` commits the current state under a temporary tag and creates\n`BOX-copy` boxes from it; the temporary image is not listed as a snapshot.\n\nSnapshots are per-machine. To move one to another host, save the image, copy\nit, load it there, then record it as a snapshot:\n\n```sh\ndocker save serbox-snapshot/work-ready:latest -o work-ready.tar\n# copy work-ready.tar to the other host, then:\ndocker load -i work-ready.tar\nserbox snapshot import serbox-snapshot/work-ready:latest --name work-ready\n```\n\n`snapshot import IMAGE --name NAME` records an image reference that is already\npresent locally or that Docker can pull; `--name` is required.\n\n## Remove\n\n```sh\nserbox snapshot rm work-ready --yes\n```\n\nThis deletes the snapshot record and its Docker image. Boxes already created\nfrom it are unaffected. Removing a box never removes its snapshots; remove\nthose explicitly when they are no longer needed.\n\n## Safety\n\n- Deleting a snapshot is irreversible. Confirm the name with `snapshot ls`\n  before running `rm`.\n- A snapshot of a box with secrets in its environment does not store the\n  environment, but files the box wrote (`.env`, tokens in config files) are\n  included. Rotate credentials before sharing an image.\n- Published ports are host configuration, not part of the snapshot; a new box\n  needs its own `port publish`.\n",
  },
]

